FROM (VALUES
  ('a147a2d8-edb7-451e-a742-12f574e992ea','How-Kota Archers, based in Pierre, South Dakota''s state capital, is an ASA-affiliated volunteer club serving archers across the state''s central plains region. South Dakota''s hunting culture runs deep, particularly around deer season on the prairie, and an ASA-affiliated club in the capital city likely draws members from a fairly wide surrounding area given how sparsely populated much of central South Dakota is. Terry Florentz is listed as the club''s contact, the person to reach for questions about shoot dates, membership, or course conditions. As is typical for volunteer-run clubs, further details on hours, dues, and day-to-day operations aren''t published publicly, so a direct inquiry is the most reliable way to get current information.'),
  ('e3d89c03-2469-412a-85b8-43c3a7f1ed4d','Howell Gun Club Archery, based in Howell, Michigan, holds USA Archery affiliation and runs a broad slate of programs for a single club: Junior Olympic Archery Development for young shooters, an adult program for grown beginners, plus both 3D and field archery for members wanting targets beyond the standard paper face. That range of formats under one roof is unusual and suggests a membership spanning recurve competitors, casual adult shooters, and archers who enjoy simulated hunting rounds. Southeast Michigan has a solid base of archery activity, and a club offering this much variety is worth a look for families weighing which program fits. Contact the club directly for schedules, fees, and current availability.'),
  ('958cb832-16ca-4d68-b016-0bca955ad0fe','HSS Sports Academy in Irvine, California operates as a USA Archery affiliated club built around Junior Olympic Archery Development, the youth pathway program that channels kids toward recurve competition through structured coaching rather than casual drop-in shooting. Orange County has a dense, competitive youth archery scene, largely fed by JOAD clubs feeding regional tournaments, so a program with this affiliation fits squarely into that pipeline. Families looking for a structured, competition-oriented introduction for a child, rather than a casual weekend outing, are the natural fit here. Specific details on coaching staff, class sizes, and enrollment aren''t listed, so reaching out directly is the way to confirm openings and cost.'),
  ('9b07d802-6f74-494c-897f-bb7ccb42b5ec','Hunt County Archery Club in Greenville, Texas is affiliated with the Archery Shooters Association, putting it in the 3D archery and bowhunting-focused circuit that a lot of North Texas clubs use to organize their shoots. ASA affiliation generally points to a membership oriented around scored rounds on realistic animal targets rather than pure target work, which tends to appeal to hunters sharpening their eye before deer season. Rob Camp is listed as a contact for the club, a good starting point for anyone who wants to ask about shoot schedules or how to join, since day-to-day details aren''t otherwise published. Greenville sits within reach of the greater Dallas area, giving the club a decent local pool to draw from.'),
  ('84b1027e-cebf-4e82-9d50-429a4cf76cb5','Huntin Hard Archers is an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club based in Happy Jack, a small community up in Arizona''s Coconino County high country known more for its ponderosa pine forest than its size. That affiliation places the club in the scored, animal-target circuit that draws bowhunters sharpening distance judgment ahead of Arizona''s elk and deer seasons rather than archers focused purely on flat-target competition. Theresa Garcia is listed as the club''s contact, worth reaching out to for questions about shoot dates or membership since nothing about hours or facilities is otherwise published. Given the remote setting, this club likely serves a fairly tight-knit group of local hunters and archers rather than a broad regional draw.'),
  ('576e1e07-b446-45e0-860d-37d15db476d0','Hunting Spot is a club listing out of Delta, Utah that carries an ASA affiliation, though the record on file notes the affiliation status as expired as of 2025, so it''s worth confirming directly whether the club is still active or has let the membership lapse. Delta sits in a sparsely populated stretch of west-central Utah where small, informal archery and bowhunting groups are common and don''t always maintain updated affiliation records. Given the expired status, anyone interested shouldn''t assume the club is currently running scored 3D shoots tied to that affiliation without checking first. The most reliable way to find out whether Hunting Spot is still meeting is to reach out locally rather than rely on the archived record.'),
  ('eed097d7-0567-4342-b71b-1608036efab9','HYEYOUN PARK JOAD ARCHERY CLUB in Cupertino, California is a USA Archery affiliated program built around Junior Olympic Archery Development, with an adult program alongside it and lessons offered on top of both, making it a genuine entry point for beginners rather than a club that only serves archers who already know how to shoot. Cupertino sits in the heart of Silicon Valley, an area with a competitive, well-resourced youth archery scene, and a JOAD club offering formal lessons fits that pattern of structured, coaching-driven programs common in the region. Parents seeking a child''s first introduction to recurve archery, or adults starting from scratch, are the clearest fit. Reach out directly for schedules and current enrollment.'),
  ('3439c26e-0e22-4b56-8557-5616b4174064','Illiana Bowhunters is an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club in Georgetown, Illinois, near the Indiana border in a region locals often call the Illiana area for its straddling of both states. The ASA affiliation puts the club in the scored, animal-target 3D circuit, a format that draws bowhunters wanting realistic practice for judging range and shot placement before deer season rather than archers focused on flat paper targets. Bill Kingore is the listed contact, a useful first call for anyone wanting details on shoot dates or how to join, since none of that is published beyond his name. East-central Illinois has a modest but consistent bowhunting culture, and a club like this gives local archers a structured place to shoot.'),
  ('1c28aee0-6dea-42b1-83a5-398506ceab69','Impact Archery of Ky is an ASA-affiliated 3D club in Williamsburg, Kentucky, tucked into the southeastern part of the state near the Tennessee border where bowhunting is deeply woven into local outdoor life. The ASA tie places the club in the scored animal-target format that bowhunters use to practice range estimation and shot placement ahead of Kentucky''s deer season, distinct from clubs built solely around flat-target competition. Brandon Shelley is listed as the contact, the person to reach for specifics on shoot dates or membership since none of that is otherwise published. Southeastern Kentucky''s mountainous terrain makes 3D courses with realistic elevation a natural fit for local hunters sharpening their skills before heading into the woods.'),
  ('54f1934a-3e72-4257-8ab3-a58380099b00','In Range Archery is an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club serving Richmond, Kentucky, a college town south of Lexington with a solid base of outdoor and hunting activity. The ASA affiliation situates the club within the scored, realistic-target 3D format that appeals mainly to bowhunters honing their skills for deer season rather than pure target competitors. Caira Aldridge is the listed contact, worth reaching out to for questions on shoot schedules and how membership works, since the listing itself doesn''t spell those details out. Richmond''s location within the Bluegrass region, close to Lexington and the edge of the Appalachian foothills, gives the club a fairly broad catchment area of local archers to draw from.'),
  ('b1dca8fe-7860-40b3-a05a-761b0c25bc83','In-Range Archery JOAD, also based in Richmond, Kentucky, is a USA Archery affiliated program that runs Junior Olympic Archery Development alongside 3D and field archery, and it operates its own pro shop on site, giving members a place to buy or service gear without leaving the facility. That combination of a structured youth pathway, multiple shooting formats, and retail support is a fuller setup than many single-focus clubs offer, likely making it a hub for competitive recurve shooters and archers who prefer 3D or field rounds. Richmond''s location in the Bluegrass region gives it access to archers from Lexington and the surrounding counties. Families interested in the JOAD program or pro shop should contact the facility directly.'),
  ('a41e99e6-c275-4094-a5e3-27c291e6a077','Inside Out Archery of KY is an ASA-affiliated 3D club based in Marion, Kentucky, in the far western part of the state near Kentucky Lake. The ASA affiliation puts it in the scored animal-target 3D circuit that western Kentucky''s bowhunting community leans on to prepare for deer season, distinct from clubs built around flat paper-target competition. Josh Orr is listed as the contact, the person to reach for shoot dates or how to get involved, since none of that is published beyond his name. The Kentucky Lake region draws a good amount of outdoor recreation traffic, and a 3D club in Marion gives local hunters and archers a dedicated place to shoot together ahead of the fall season.'),
  ('c810a806-095a-4157-8dea-d9fd9a49c208','Integrity Archery of Florida, based in Orlando, is a USA Archery affiliated club running both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program for young shooters and an adult program alongside it, covering both ends of the age spectrum under one roof. Orlando''s large population and tourist economy support a broad recreational sports scene, and a club offering structured pathways for kids and adults fits a city where families often look for organized, coached activities rather than informal shooting. The dual JOAD and adult programming suggests a facility built for teaching fundamentals rather than one that only serves archers who already compete. Class schedules and fees aren''t listed, so reaching out directly is the way to check availability.'),
  ('5a540d75-458d-4d4a-9fe8-47fd0cb79d43','Invictus Archery in San Jose, California runs as a USA Archery affiliated club offering both Junior Olympic Archery Development for kids and a separate adult program, giving the South Bay a structured option for archers at very different starting points. San Jose sits at the heart of a competitive Bay Area youth archery scene, with JOAD clubs frequently feeding regional tournaments and, for some athletes, a path toward collegiate competition. Pairing that youth pipeline with an adult program broadens the club''s reach beyond families with kids in the sport to adults picking up a bow for the first time. Coaching staff, class sizes, and current enrollment aren''t listed, so contacting the club directly is the way to check availability.'),
  ('59a2e88f-fb33-45cf-accd-84b075054e4e','Ipswich Fish And Game Association, on Massachusetts''s North Shore, is a USA Archery affiliated club that layers a fair amount onto its archery program: Junior Olympic Archery Development for younger shooters, an adult program, a 3D course for members who want to shoot animal targets through the woods, and lessons for people starting from zero. Fish and game associations like this one are common across New England and typically bundle archery in alongside hunting, fishing, and conservation activities, giving members access to a broader outdoors community. That range of offerings, especially the pairing of formal lessons with a 3D course, makes it a reasonably complete option for archers of any experience level. Contact the association directly for schedules.'),
  ('7231fbc4-722d-40a0-bd68-67f331241659','Iron Draw Archery in Statesboro, Georgia, home to Georgia Southern University, is a USA Archery affiliated club running a wide spread of programming: Junior Olympic Archery Development, an adult program, 3D archery, and field archery all under one club. That breadth of formats is more than most single clubs offer and suggests a membership base spanning youth competitors, adult beginners, and archers who prefer the more varied 3D and field disciplines over standard target rounds. Statesboro''s college-town setting, combined with the surrounding rural southeast Georgia countryside, likely brings in both a student population and a broader regional hunting community. Anyone interested should reach out to the club directly, since specific schedules and enrollment details aren''t listed here.'),
  ('fc765118-eb7c-4f15-89b5-761b07c14c89','Island Archers, on Bainbridge Island in Washington''s Puget Sound just a ferry ride from Seattle, is a USA Archery affiliated club running Junior Olympic Archery Development, an adult program, and 3D archery together, giving the island community a fairly complete range of options in one place. Bainbridge Island''s relatively small, close-knit population means a club covering youth, adult, and 3D shooting likely serves as the primary local archery hub rather than one of several competing options, as might be the case in a larger metro area. That combination of a formal youth pathway with adult and 3D programming suggests a club built to bring in newcomers as easily as it retains experienced shooters. Reach out directly for schedules and coaching availability.'),
  ('f5e9b238-e5f2-47b2-93bc-59c698a979d8','Island Hilltop Archery is an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club in Sicily Island, a small community in northeastern Louisiana known for its high ground rising above the surrounding bottomlands, hence the name. The ASA tie puts the club within the scored, realistic animal-target 3D format that Louisiana''s bowhunting community relies on to prepare for the state''s deer season, distinct from a club built around flat target competition. Barry Jenkins is the listed contact, the person to reach out to for shoot schedules or membership questions, since the listing doesn''t spell out day-to-day operations beyond that. Sicily Island''s rural, wooded setting along the Mississippi flyway region makes it a fitting spot for a 3D course built around natural terrain and realistic hunting scenarios.'),
  ('94715022-c55d-44ea-b951-0274fbe32e6d','USA Archery affiliation anchors Ithaca Archery''s approach, and the club backs that up with two distinct tracks: a Junior Olympic Archery Development program for younger competitors building toward tournament form, and an Adult Archery Program aimed at grown-ups picking up a bow for the first time. Ithaca''s college-town population, with Cornell and Ithaca College both nearby, means a steady rotation of newcomers looking for real instruction rather than unsupervised range time, and lessons being part of the package fits that need directly. The Finger Lakes region doesn''t have many USA Archery clubs running a full JOAD pipeline, so this is a genuine resource for local families. Contact the club for current class schedules and enrollment details.'),
  ('0d27cf60-2632-4522-831a-9972ffa648b9','Jaat Archery in Upper Sandusky is listed in the IBO directory as a commercial range, which places it inside the International Bowhunting Organization''s network of 3D-style shooting venues rather than a casual retail counter with a lane in back. Upper Sandusky sits in north-central Ohio, an area with a solid bowhunting culture, and an IBO-recognized commercial operation there likely draws archers tuning up for 3D shoots and hunting season alike. Beyond the IBO listing itself, no further detail on lanes, lessons, or a pro shop is confirmed for this location. Archers in the region who want specifics on course layout, hours, or upcoming events should contact Jaat Archery directly rather than assume standard commercial-range amenities apply.'),
  ('29065cb4-b979-4ce0-a846-6216f0ae023e','Jackson Bowhunters is an ASA-affiliated 3D archery club based in Jackson, in the hill country of southeastern Ohio, putting it inside the Archery Shooters Association''s competitive circuit built around lifelike animal targets over uneven terrain. That affiliation generally signals a group organized around scored 3D rounds and a bowhunting-minded membership rather than flat-range target shooting alone. Kenneth Moon is listed as the club''s contact, a useful starting point for anyone wanting to know about shoot dates or course conditions, since the club doesn''t appear to publish that information more broadly. Southeastern Ohio''s terrain suits this kind of course well. Reach out to Kenneth Moon directly for specifics on membership and schedules.'),
  ('7c247076-b8c9-462d-b199-bffe11efee69','An ASA affiliation and a confirmed 3D course put Jackson County Outdoor Club squarely in the realistic-target, bowhunting-oriented end of the archery world, based out of Jackson in south-central Michigan. Clubs carrying the ASA badge typically run scored shoots across animal-shaped targets set through wooded terrain, which tracks with the outdoor club structure suggested by the name here. Max McFeters is listed as the contact for the club, the right person to ask about shoot schedules or membership, since specifics beyond the 3D course and ASA tie aren''t otherwise published. South-central Michigan has plenty of hunting land, and a club like this one likely serves as a seasonal gathering point for local bowhunters.'),
  ('6a7e3e35-02ec-4f14-ab74-4cf1d9685831','Jackson Parish Bowhunters carries an ASA affiliation and calls Jonesboro, in north-central Louisiana, home, placing it among the state''s 3D archery clubs built around scored shoots at animal-shaped targets rather than conventional bullseye rounds. Louisiana''s bowhunting season draws heavily on clubs exactly like this one to keep members'' form and equipment tuned through the off-season, and the ASA tie usually means a course laid out over realistic, wooded terrain. Heath Hall is the listed contact, worth reaching out to directly for shoot dates, course conditions, or how to join, since the club doesn''t appear to have much else published beyond that. For archers in the Jonesboro area with a bowhunting bent, this looks like a natural local option to explore.'),
  ('6bf10d57-0dc0-4128-bacc-264d9bc8f460','Jay County Bitteridge Archers, based in Portland in east-central Indiana, is listed in the NFAA Club/Range Finder, which places it inside the National Field Archery Association''s network rather than the 3D-focused ASA or Olympic-style USA Archery circuits. NFAA affiliation usually points toward field and target archery traditions, including field rounds shot across varied outdoor terrain, though the specific programs this club runs aren''t spelled out beyond the listing itself. Jay County is a rural stretch of the state near the Ohio border, and a club with this kind of affiliation is a solid marker of an established, organized group. Anyone interested should get in touch directly for shoot schedules and membership information.'),
  ('95425fd6-2264-4d72-8787-e55ab63861b8','Jefferson County Bowhunters, out of Mt Olive just outside Birmingham, is an ASA-affiliated club, which means its shoots are built around scored 3D targets and a bowhunting-focused membership rather than conventional flat-range archery. Central Alabama has a deep bowhunting tradition, and clubs carrying the ASA badge tend to serve as a season-long tune-up circuit for hunters as much as a competitive outlet for target archers. James Hornbuckle is listed as the contact, the person to reach for questions about course conditions, shoot dates, or joining, since the club doesn''t appear to publish much beyond that. For archers around Mt Olive and the greater Birmingham area, this looks like a natural local option for realistic 3D practice ahead of hunting season.'),
  ('b9e740aa-53ba-4f0e-b48c-f499eb8c8f9c','Festus, south of St. Louis along the Mississippi River, is home to Jefferson County Bowmen, an ASA-affiliated club that puts it in the same 3D archery and bowhunting circuit used by a lot of clubs across the Midwest. That affiliation generally means shoots set up around lifelike animal targets across natural terrain rather than a flat indoor range, appealing to hunters keeping their form sharp between seasons. Nelson Scherrer is the listed contact for the club, worth reaching out to for details on shoot schedules or membership, since public information beyond the ASA tie is limited. Archers in the Jefferson County area looking for a 3D-focused group should start with a direct message to Nelson.'),
  ('a576df45-5995-496d-9ca4-100f0c1195f7','Jefferson County Sportsmen''s Club in Mount Washington, just south of Louisville, carries an ASA affiliation, aligning it with the Archery Shooters Association''s circuit of scored 3D shoots rather than standard target archery. Bullitt County sits in a part of Kentucky with strong deer hunting traditions, and a sportsmen''s club with this affiliation likely functions as both a competitive outlet and a practical off-season tune-up spot for local bowhunters. Colby Murphy is listed as the point of contact, the right person to ask about course conditions or how to become a member, since little else about day-to-day operations is publicly listed. Anyone near Mount Washington curious about 3D archery should reach out to Colby directly.'),
  ('b26ffad0-3e44-4bf0-98d8-932ef4c175e9','Joliet Archery Club, actually based in New Lenox southwest of Chicago, is a USA Archery affiliated club running three programs at once: Junior Olympic Archery Development for younger competitive shooters, an Adult Archery Program for grown-ups getting started or coming back to the sport, and Field Archery for those who want to shoot varied distances across natural terrain rather than a flat line. That combination is broader than most single-focus clubs in the Chicago suburbs, giving members a path from beginner instruction into more specialized formats without switching organizations. Will County has a sizable population to draw from. Contact the club for current schedules and enrollment.'),
  ('4bb52351-374e-4174-ad1b-f3a4f12761ec','Junior Olympian Archery Club of Louisville is actually based in Simpsonville, a growing town east of the city in Shelby County, and carries a USA Archery affiliation with both a Junior Olympic Archery Development track and an Adult Archery Program running alongside it. The JOAD name signals a club built around Olympic-style recurve and compound shooting, but the adult program means it isn''t exclusively a youth pipeline, giving grown-ups in the Louisville metro a structured entry point too. Shelby County has seen steady suburban growth, and a club with this kind of dual programming is a solid option for families. Reach out directly for class schedules and enrollment.'),
  ('ffa9de57-0403-4c4a-8e6a-10bc8aa51705','K Archery Club in Cumming, part of the fast-growing Forsyth County area north of Atlanta, holds a USA Archery affiliation built specifically around a Junior Olympic Archery Development program rather than a broader mix of adult or 3D offerings. That narrower focus suggests a club oriented toward younger archers working through structured, competitive-track instruction rather than a catch-all community range. Forsyth County''s population has boomed over the last decade, and a dedicated JOAD program there fills a real need for local families. No other programs are listed for K Archery Club, so parents should contact the club directly for age groups, schedules, and cost.'),
  ('360d8f93-e944-42fe-8ac9-415f2434065f','Kennesaw Archery Club is actually located in Acworth, a bit north of Kennesaw itself in the fast-growing Cobb-Cherokee county corridor, and carries a USA Archery affiliation covering Junior Olympic Archery Development, an Adult Archery Program, and Field Archery all under one roof. That range of programs gives the club a genuine full pipeline, from youth competitors working toward Olympic-style form to adults picking up a bow for the first time to members who want field rounds. Metro Atlanta''s northwest suburbs have grown rapidly, and a club offering this much structure is a strong option for families. Anyone interested should contact the club directly for current class times.'),
  ('68478130-49c8-4b97-b5f9-c20ad46c3fc7','Kenosha Bowmen, based in Bristol near the Illinois state line in southeastern Wisconsin, runs one of the more fully built-out programs in this data set, combining USA Archery affiliation with Junior Olympic Archery Development, an Adult Archery Program, 3D Archery, and Field Archery, backed by confirmed 3D and field courses on site. That breadth covers Olympic-style target work, realistic 3D shooting, and varied-terrain field rounds in a single club, which is unusual and suggests a well-established organization with real course infrastructure. Southeastern Wisconsin sits within reach of both Milwaukee and Chicago, giving Kenosha Bowmen a large potential membership base. Archers interested in any of these formats should reach out directly for schedules.'),
  ('aa8bdeb3-b1f0-4a4b-b55b-233d38aece4d','Kenton Game & Fish Assoc. is listed in the IBO directory as a pro shop, located at Locust Pike in Kentucky, which places it inside the International Bowhunting Organization''s network of equipment and service providers rather than a course or range venue in its own right. A game and fish association name usually points to roots in a broader conservation or sportsmen''s organization, with the pro shop functioning as one piece of that operation. No detail is confirmed here on lanes, a course, or lessons, so the IBO pro shop listing is the main confirmed fact about this location. Archers in the area should contact Kenton Game & Fish Assoc. directly to find out what services are currently available.'),
  ('0fbcb249-8882-4396-b951-d461d9b1e051','Kentucky Elite Archery Academy in Ashland, along the Ohio River in the state''s northeastern corner, pairs a USA Archery affiliation with both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and 3D Archery, plus confirmed lessons, giving members a route into competitive Olympic-style shooting and 3D target work under the same roof. The academy framing suggests an operation built around structured instruction rather than a casual drop-in range. Ashland sits in a tri-state area bordering Ohio and West Virginia, and an academy offering this range of programs likely pulls members from all three states. Families or adult archers should contact the academy directly for current class schedules and enrollment.'),
  ('f2396bfa-4d5d-43ef-a8c5-4804b7960b77','Kestrel Archery in Dracut, just south of the New Hampshire line in the Merrimack Valley, brings together a USA Archery affiliation, both Junior Olympic Archery Development and Adult Archery Program tracks, a 12-lane range, an on-site pro shop, and lessons, making it one of the more fully equipped facilities in this batch. That combination means members can buy or tune gear, take structured instruction, and shoot in the same space, whether they''re a kid working toward competitive form or an adult trying archery for the first time. A facility this complete is a notable draw for the wider Lowell-area community. Anyone interested in lessons, gear, or membership should contact Kestrel Archery directly.'),
  ('a2202362-114c-467f-8567-615d45157865','Killshot Outdoors in Dexter, a small community in southeastern New Mexico''s Pecos Valley, is an ASA-affiliated volunteer club that also offers lessons, an unusual pairing since ASA clubs typically lean toward established 3D shooters and bowhunters rather than beginner instruction. That combination suggests Killshot Outdoors is building its membership base by bringing newcomers in through lessons before funneling them into the club''s 3D and bowhunting-oriented shoots. Robbie DeRosier is listed as the contact, the person to reach for lesson availability or membership questions, since the club doesn''t appear to publish much else publicly. Southeastern New Mexico''s hunting-heavy culture makes this a natural fit for the area. Anyone interested should reach out to Robbie directly.'),
