  ('472636ea-69e6-4940-a5fd-9aa3d4fd3362','Kishwaukee Archers in Sycamore, Illinois is affiliated with USA Archery and runs both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and an Adult Archery Program, giving the club a genuine pathway for shooters at different stages rather than a one-size-fits-all setup. JOAD programs follow USA Archery''s structured coaching curriculum, so families in this part of northern Illinois looking for a serious youth pipeline have a real option here, alongside adult offerings for people picking up the sport later. Beyond the two named programs, specifics on facilities, course type, or schedule aren''t listed. Interested archers, especially parents of prospective JOAD athletes, should contact the club directly for enrollment details.'),
  ('a027350e-9a21-4f28-a4f9-9b85195600da','Koteewi Archery in Noblesville, Indiana pairs an ASA-affiliated 3D course with an on-site pro shop and lessons, a fuller setup than most volunteer clubs manage to offer. The 3D affiliation puts it in the scored, animal-target format that draws a bowhunting-minded crowd across central Indiana, while the pro shop means archers can likely handle basic gear needs without a separate stop, and the lesson option opens the door to newer shooters rather than just experienced club members. Tony Girt is the listed contact for anyone wanting specifics on shoot schedules or lesson availability. Given the range of offerings here, contacting the club directly is worth it before planning a visit.'),
  ('a50fa617-3ac7-4842-9b99-a85aab5c39fd','KSL Archery Academy operates out of Van Nuys in the San Fernando Valley as a USA Archery affiliated club, running both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and an Adult Archery Program for people starting later. The JOAD pathway follows USA Archery''s national coaching framework, so families in the Los Angeles area looking for a structured, competition-oriented track for younger archers have a real option in this academy rather than a casual drop-in setup. The adult program suggests the academy isn''t only built around youth development. Facility details like course type or lane count aren''t listed, so anyone interested in enrolling should contact the academy directly for current class schedules.'),
