  ('b7949529-7d55-46f6-92f9-e799e1b5c8f2','McDonald Youth Archery, in the small Washington County town of McDonald southwest of Pittsburgh, puts its focus right in the name, running a USA Archery-affiliated Junior Olympic Archery Development program alongside a 3D archery course. Combining a JOAD pathway with 3D shooting is a somewhat unusual pairing, giving younger archers exposure to both Olympic-style target technique and the animal-target, bowhunting-adjacent format in one program. Southwestern Pennsylvania''s steel-town-turned-suburban communities around Pittsburgh have a decent base of families looking for structured youth sports options, and a dedicated youth archery program fills a specific niche there. No adult program or facility details are listed, so contacting the program directly is the way to learn more about signing a young archer up.'),
  ('5db68b1f-2196-43be-ac21-97d80adcc788','McHenry Parks & Recreation runs a USA Archery-affiliated Junior Olympic Archery Development program as part of its municipal recreation offerings in McHenry, Illinois, northwest of Chicago. Parks and recreation departments running JOAD programs is a model seen in a number of towns, folding archery into the same public system that handles youth sports leagues and community classes rather than leaving it to a private club. McHenry County''s mix of suburban development and remaining farmland supports a decent population base for a municipal program to draw from. Enrollment likely happens through the town''s standard registration process, though session times and costs aren''t listed, so checking with the department directly is the next step.'),
  ('490d25f4-d1ae-488b-a9df-a1f8a44d1118','Meade County Archery serves bowhunters and target shooters in Bradenburg, Kentucky, and appears in the International Bowhunters Organization''s pro shop directory, signaling a working relationship with the IBO 3D competition community. As a commercial operation, it''s built around walk-in customers rather than a members-only club structure, making it a reasonable first stop for archers new to the area or passing through north-central Kentucky. Specific details on hours, lane setup, and current inventory aren''t listed here, so anyone planning a visit, whether for equipment, tuning, or range time, should contact Meade County Archery directly to confirm what''s currently available before making the trip.'),
  ('da159aa1-fc16-4819-a471-41e59c987df1','Menard Archers is a volunteer-run 3D archery club based in Petersburg, Illinois, affiliated with the Archery Shooters Association. That ASA tie puts the club squarely in the 3D and bowhunting-practice tradition, with foam animal targets set at unmarked distances to sharpen the kind of range estimation hunters rely on in the field. As a member-driven club rather than a commercial range, Menard Archers is likely to lean on volunteer labor and member dues to keep the course maintained. Gary Sumpter is listed as a contact for the club, a good starting point for anyone in the Petersburg area wanting to shoot the course or ask about joining.'),
  ('12e434ef-151a-4654-ab09-129cdd6d6915','Mesquite Archery Club, located in Terrell, Texas, has carried an Archery Shooters Association affiliation, tying it into the 3D competitive archery and bowhunting-practice scene common across the state. That ASA status is listed as expired for 2025, so the affiliation may currently be lapsed or up for renewal rather than active. As a club rather than a commercial range, it''s organized around its own membership rather than public retail hours. Given the uncertainty around its current ASA standing, archers interested in Mesquite Archery Club, whether for competition, casual shooting, or membership, should contact the club directly to confirm what''s currently active before planning a visit.'),
  ('e0ae415a-c5b6-435c-a55c-c1305e2b7c70','Metropolitan Rod & Gun Club brings organized archery to Brooklyn, New York as a USA Archery affiliated club running both a Junior Olympic Archery Development program and an Adult Archery Program. That combination means the club serves young shooters working toward Olympic-style competition alongside adults picking up the sport for the first time, a useful pairing for a dense urban borough where standalone archery facilities are scarce. As a hybrid operation, it blends club structure with broader outdoor recreation typical of a rod and gun club. Archers in the Brooklyn area interested in JOAD or adult sessions should reach out to Metropolitan Rod & Gun Club directly for current schedules and enrollment.'),
  ('b309f6d9-dab6-412c-8090-169dbda417b0','Miami Archery Club, based in Homestead, Florida, runs an unusually broad slate of USA Archery affiliated programming: Junior Olympic Archery Development for young competitors, 3D and field archery for hunters and outdoor-format shooters, and an Olympic Archery in the Schools program that brings the sport into local classrooms. That range of offerings suggests a club actively building the sport''s next generation across South Florida rather than just maintaining a single course. As a hybrid facility, it likely combines club membership with a broader community reach. Families and archers in the Homestead and greater Miami area should contact the club directly for current enrollment and schedules across its programs.'),
  ('608844b8-dde7-4130-9ad6-e549508c2025','Michiana Archery in South Bend, Indiana pairs USA Archery affiliated Junior Olympic Archery Development and Adult Archery programming with the practical extras that make a facility easy to actually use: an on-site pro shop and lessons alongside a 10-lane range. That combination, coaching, retail, and dedicated lane space, points to a facility built to take a shooter from a first lesson through steady practice without needing to travel elsewhere for equipment or instruction. It''s a solid option for South Bend-area families looking to start kids in JOAD or for adults picking up a bow for the first time. Contact Michiana Archery directly for current lesson schedules, lane availability, and pro shop hours.'),
  ('704e7713-34c6-44f5-b89d-dc8067517a75','Mid GA Archery Club, based in Perry, Georgia, is a USA Archery affiliated club offering both Junior Olympic Archery Development for young competitors and an Adult Archery Program for grown-up beginners, backed by lessons for those just getting started. That structure makes it a genuine entry point rather than a members-only course for archers who already know what they''re doing. Perry sits in central Georgia, giving the club a reasonable draw from the surrounding region. Anyone interested in getting a child into JOAD or picking up archery as an adult should contact Mid GA Archery Club directly to find out current lesson availability and how to enroll.'),
  ('06315a01-d040-45b9-988e-7a180fca722b','Mid Nebraska Bowhunters, located in Litchfield, Nebraska, is a USA Archery affiliated club running an Adult Archery Program, aimed squarely at grown-up archers rather than a youth pipeline. The bowhunter-focused name suggests a membership that leans toward hunting practice alongside target work, a common overlap in rural Nebraska archery clubs. As a hybrid facility, it likely combines club-style membership with a broader recreational or hunting community base. Litchfield is a small community, so the club probably draws archers from a fair stretch of central Nebraska rather than just the town itself. Adults interested in joining or getting involved should contact Mid Nebraska Bowhunters directly for current program details and schedules.'),
  ('85a7ad6f-37f9-481d-a3d5-85c0d7e017f0','Midlands Archery Center in Leesville, South Carolina is a USA Archery affiliated facility running Junior Olympic Archery Development, an Adult Archery Program, and 3D archery, backed by a 30-lane range and its own 3D course. That''s a genuinely broad setup, spanning youth Olympic-style training, adult beginners, and outdoor 3D format shooting, all under one roof and grounds. The lane count alone puts it among the larger facilities in the area, suggesting real capacity for group sessions, leagues, or busy weekend traffic. For archers in the Leesville or Midlands, South Carolina region looking for youth programs, adult instruction, or 3D practice, Midlands Archery Center is worth a direct call to check current schedules and availability.'),
  ('0c9d32ec-4f1b-4039-a9df-4d9ab11396a9','Midwest Mavericks Archery, based in Farmersburg, Indiana, is a USA Archery affiliated club running a Junior Olympic Archery Development program, putting its focus squarely on young archers working toward Olympic-recurve style competition. Farmersburg is a small community in western Indiana, so the club likely draws JOAD families from a broader stretch of the Wabash Valley rather than just the town itself. As a hybrid facility, it probably blends structured club programming with a more general recreational base. Details on adult programs, lane count, or additional formats aren''t listed here. Parents or young archers interested in JOAD should contact Midwest Mavericks Archery directly for current enrollment and practice schedules.'),
  ('8451162e-aa12-453f-be00-ed6bc81f435b','Midwest Open Indoor Archery is a volunteer-run club in Springfield, Illinois carrying an Archery Shooters Association affiliation, which is notable given the club''s name leans indoor while ASA affiliation is typically tied to 3D and bowhunting-practice competition outdoors; the two may reflect a club that runs both indoor sessions and outdoor 3D involvement. Kara Kuhnert is listed as a contact, a useful starting point for anyone in the Springfield area wanting to shoot with the club or ask about its current format. As a volunteer organization, it likely runs on member involvement rather than paid staff. Reach out directly to confirm current indoor hours, 3D activity, and membership options.'),
  ('48a92738-96f1-45c3-a9d9-6b35b976d1be','Mile High Archers, based in Denver, Colorado, is a USA Archery affiliated club running an unusually full program lineup: Junior Olympic Archery Development, an Adult Archery Program, 3D archery, and field archery. That breadth covers youth Olympic-style training, adult beginners, and both major outdoor formats, making it a genuine hub option for archers across the Denver metro rather than a single-format club. Given the name, it likely serves a wide catchment across the Front Range rather than just the city itself. Archers interested in any of these programs, from getting a kid started in JOAD to shooting 3D or field rounds as an adult, should contact Mile High Archers directly for current schedules.'),
  ('7115737b-64c4-429f-892e-8b93e640abf4','Mill River Archery in Amherst, Massachusetts is a USA Archery affiliated club offering Junior Olympic Archery Development, an Adult Archery Program, and lessons, giving it a clear on-ramp for both kids aiming at competitive Olympic-style shooting and adults trying the sport for the first time. Amherst''s location in the Pioneer Valley, home to several colleges, likely brings in a mix of student, family, and longtime local archers. The combination of youth and adult programming alongside instruction suggests a facility built around teaching rather than just providing range time to already-experienced shooters. Anyone in the Amherst area interested in JOAD, adult sessions, or lessons should contact Mill River Archery directly for current schedules.')
) AS v(id, description)
WHERE r.id = v.id::uuid AND r.is_claimed = false;
